title: "Bounded swaps in pass-and-swap queues: counterexamples to a conjecture of Dorsman and Gardner, and a proof for bipartite swapping graphs with odd caps under positive service rates"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Anonymous
version: 1.0.0-candidate
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23515841
date-released: 2026-10-20
repository-code: "https://github.com/ipitchford/pass-and-swap-bounded-swaps"
url: "https://evidencepress.org/releases/pass-and-swap-bounded-swaps/"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - pass-and-swap queues
  - product-form stationary distribution
  - order-independent queues
  - acyclic orientations
  - promotion on linear extensions
  - counterexample
abstract: "Counterexamples, for every swap cap w >= 2, to Conjecture 1 of Dorsman and Gardner (2024) on closed tandems of pass-and-swap queues; an exact classification on cycles (n = 1 mod 2w, under positive rates); a two-odd-cycle family; a census of all connected graphs with at most seven vertices; a proof of the conjecture for bipartite swapping graphs with odd caps under positive rates; and stationary laws on the counterexample class. Unrefereed candidate with exact replayable verifiers. Original code is MIT-licensed; see LICENSES.md."
